/* @catalog — generated by `npm run catalog:generate`; do not edit by hand.
 * Internal
 *   Functions: stubFetch, mount, createServer, entriesServer, decidedProject
 *   Constants: unticked, changedElsewhere
 * Tests
 *   - workbench distinguishes confirmed empty from failed load and does not query in User view
 *   - manual edits save only the private draft and never start analysis or publication
 *   - refresh retains unsaved changes until explicitly loading a newer saved version
 *   - A to B route owns a new mutation and cannot show or retry the earlier project
 *   - file-only intake needs no folder name and Create starts one sequential upload per file
 *   - the New import page explains the public default and creates the import without a draft
 *   - folder intake keeps the editable folder name
 *   - an upload that bumps the revision keeps unsaved edits without a conflict
 *   - a view change between Create and its confirmation stops the queue before any file is sent, and Resume uploads them
 *   - a Create confirmed after leaving its page still starts the approved uploads, and New import later opens a fresh form
 *   - an outdated save response asks for a page reload and offers no retry of the original intent
 *   - a project saved by a newer release refuses a save with a reload request for that action only
 *   - an append to an Album without a primary Artist explains the refusal instead of a generic conflict, with no retry
 *   - cancelled publication cleanup permits manual review while analysis and source mutations stay blocked
 *   - stage navigation keeps private edits and selected suggestions without a mutation
 *   - workbench refresh stays in its header while personal filtering remains with search
 *   - catalog reviews are a separate read-only workbench source with search, owner filtering and cursor paging
 *   - the catalog review empty state distinguishes confirmed absence from a failed load
 *   - returning to the catalog review source reads that queue without querying imports or starting analysis
 *   - catalog review Unfinished filtering preserves the private queue contract without suggesting creation on no matches
 *   - completed catalog reviews describe applied changes rather than an import publication
 *   - an unfinished Album completion card offers Discard completion naming its catalog Album; confirming reads the queue again without the card, a running Luna AI disables it, and an applied card offers none
 *   - a card whose review page left a change with an unknown outcome keeps Discard completion disabled until that change is confirmed
 *   - the project edit action opens Draft even after a prior Review visit and sends no mutation
 *   - Add Artist and a typed name save one primary entry as the only change, and a rename keeps its key
 *   - several Artist entries are editable in order, and the header shows their byline
 *   - a save refused because another administrator changed that value loads the saved version for comparison, with no retry
 *   - a track edit keeps its saved Disc Number and sends only the changed title, and edits reverted to the saved values leave nothing to save
 *   - an unsaved buffer of the earlier v1 editor is never read as the Draft v2 draft
 *   - clearing the Artist name and retyping the saved name leaves nothing to save, an empty name sends nothing, and a new name keeps the saved entry
 *   - another administrator saving a different value rebases unsaved edits: Save stays available and sends only this editor's value
 *   - automatic values written at the same revision rebase unsaved edits without a conflict, and an edit over an automatic value is kept
 *   - an editor without unsaved edits takes automatic values written at the same revision and marks them From file tags
 *   - a Disc Number typed in the import editor is saved as the only change
 *   - reordering Artist entries by keyboard saves the reordered list as the only change, keeping each key and role and each phrase in its position
 *   - a role change and a label edit save only album.artists and album.label, and clearing the label saves no label
 *   - an edited entry list with duplicate names sends no save until the names differ
 *   - a draft of two primaries, a featured entry and a label is decided entry by entry in Review and published in one step, linking every confirmed identity
 *   - an unsaved title edit is published in one request without Save, the editor then shows it saved, and Publish alone stays available while the draft is unsaved
 *   - the import page opens on the Review and publish summary above its four sections, and the summary's Publish approves the unsaved edit with the ticks it shows
 *   - an approval refused while metadata lookup runs explains it with its own message and no retry, and reads the project and its summary again
 *   - unsaved decisions save with the revision of their first edit through Luna progress, and go stale once another administrator saves decisions
 *   - a decision save refused because its entry was renamed meanwhile reloads the project and marks the unsaved decisions stale, with no retry
 *   - a refused approval keeps the unsaved edits and the Review decisions for another look
 *   - after a stale approval the page reloads the saved project, and approving again sends its new digest with the same unsaved edit
 *   - another administrator saving different Artist entries refuses this editor's entry edits and offers the saved version
 *   - a label saved elsewhere rebases unsaved entry edits, and Save sends only album.artists
 *   - MusicBrainz IDs metadata lookup added to the saved entries rebase unsaved entry edits, and Save keeps the IDs
 *   - a lost response for an entry save retries the identical intent
 *   - unsaved Artist entries and label survive leaving and reopening the project, and an account change drops them
 * @end-catalog */

